{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:sec:PURPOSE", "content_sha256": "cdd4f7893736b5fddd71fdc00087b69a19339bf1ee730d03acdae45ffa4dd7c5", "heading": "Purpose", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "# PRO-04 — Decision Points"}
{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:sec:PURPOSE", "content_sha256": "4ae7b49adbe31668dccd29fbf1d8d9d2bbdf8892dc7b1d4ec15f26113f0f4e1e", "heading": "Purpose", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Purpose\n\nThis artifact catalogues the decision points of record in 4CH1 problem solving:\nthe forks the official mark schemes publish (equipment and reagent identity\nalternatives, reverse-argument routes, observation ranges with tolerances,\ndependency and error-carried-forward rules), the which-style item type that\nforces a decision of SRC-QPMS-4CH1 and SRC-SPEC-4CH1, and the book's own decision\nrules (SRC-BOOK-4CH1-SB1). Claims ride only on this artifact's own bounded pack\nexcerpts. Canonical planes are untouched."}
{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:sec:SCOPE", "content_sha256": "7bb0792cd9545c13d1dadd1d9fc61871382aa818d47cb76f9528b58f1aeb96f3", "heading": "Scope", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Scope\n\n**Covers:** identity forks with ALLOW/ACCEPT alternates; reverse-argument\nroute forks; observation-range tolerances; dependency (DEP) and error-carried-\nforward (ECF) decision structures; which-decision items; book-side phase\ndecision rule.\n\n**Out of scope:** multi-step chains (PRO-03) and dead ends (PRO-05)."}
{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:sec:EXECUTIVE_SUMMARY", "content_sha256": "f0996e8e70c14f53f630ae89741ac0ed9a651683aa1e99485791099bc9df8553", "heading": "Executive Summary", "kind": "section", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "", "text": "## Executive Summary\n\nDecision points in 4CH1 are published with their tolerated alternatives. Where\nan identity decision arises — which piece of apparatus, which reagent, which\nname — the mark scheme prints the fork explicitly: pipette with burette\nallowed, barium chloride with the nitrate accepted, magnesium with its symbol.\nWhere a route decision arises, both directions are pre-authorised (reverse\narguments accepted on the extraction-method justification). Observation\ndecisions come with tolerance ranges (any orange/yellow combination; pink-brown\nspanning red-brown). The decision machinery also carries its own logic rules:\ndependencies (a mark depends on its parent) and error-carried-forward windows\nwith stated validity conditions. The book's phase rule shows the same\ndecision-point structure on the learning side: one rule, three regions."}
