{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:rec:PRO-021", "content_sha256": "8d617ff82ef9a5f61f493661027076aa8ffc6be6882f3d9b45ea1a0e3d119e6b", "heading": "PRO-021", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "PRO-021", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "PRO-021", "text": "### PRO-021 — Identity forks published with alternates\n\n**Claim:** identity decisions in answers carry published alternates — either\nthe apparatus or its acceptable substitute, either the name or the formula.\n**Evidence:** the apparatus item accepts \"(graduated) pipette ALLOW burette\"\n(SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 611-625); the element answer\nis \"magnesium ALLOW Mg\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines\n154-168); the sulfate test reads \"add barium chloride/BaCl2 ACCEPT barium\nnitrate/Ba(NO3)2\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 593-607).\nTemporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:rec:PRO-022", "content_sha256": "36802e5d54e72070222ad7d8bc18d17318e84f0ab24a395b9bbc76090b0a2a64", "heading": "PRO-022", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "PRO-022", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "PRO-022", "text": "### PRO-022 — Route forks with reverse arguments authorised\n\n**Claim:** method-choice decisions are pre-authorised in both directions where\nthe reasoning supports either orientation.\n**Evidence:** the extraction-method scheme marks \"Method 1/ heating the metal\noxide/lead(II) oxide with carbon\" as the chosen route and prints \"ACCEPT\nreverse arguments\" for the justification (SRC-QPMS-4CH1,\n2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 186-205). Temporal scope: CURRENT —\nAUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:rec:PRO-023", "content_sha256": "9d3e927d90ea314f707b71d58cf4f5714a498a86db49c8c57cba9b26ddbdd358", "heading": "PRO-023", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "PRO-023", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "PRO-023", "text": "### PRO-023 — Observation decisions with tolerance ranges\n\n**Claim:** observation decisions carry explicit tolerance ranges rather than a\nsingle accepted answer.\n**Evidence:** the bromine-water decision accepts \"from orange to colourless\nALLOW yellow for orange or any combination of orange/yellow\"\n(SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 407-427); the reversible\nequation decision accepts the reverse arrow while ignoring an added catalyst\nsymbol on either side (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines\n378-383). Temporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:rec:PRO-024", "content_sha256": "6f4622215bc921274f7e303b12280274a8af6beb3d3e94fbc21e277be19151cf", "heading": "PRO-024", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "PRO-024", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "PRO-024", "text": "### PRO-024 — Dependency and error-carried-forward decision structures\n\n**Claim:** the mark machinery encodes decision dependencies — a mark may depend\non its parent, and early errors carry forward only within stated validity\nconditions.\n**Evidence:** the ion-identity scheme marks the precipitate \"M2 DEP M1\"\n(SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 601-615); the chromatography\nRf scheme allows \"ECF from M1 M2 only if Rf < 1\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1,\n2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 122-136); the bond-energy scheme carries\n\"M3 M4 ECF from M1 and M2\" (SRC-QPMS-4CH1, 2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines\n433-453). Temporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:rec:PRO-025", "content_sha256": "863020f0fe486753099845477a60e32158c21158259d24494e1d63298e359c65", "heading": "PRO-025", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "PRO-025", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "PRO-025", "text": "### PRO-025 — Which-decision items\n\n**Claim:** the papers force decisions with which-style items, backed by the\ncommand-word taxonomy's maintained definitions.\n**Evidence:** a cathode-gas item asks \"Which of these tests shows that the gas\nformed at the cathode is hydrogen?\" as a keyed multiple choice (SRC-QPMS-4CH1,\n2020-11/4CH1-2C/questions.md lines 560-574); the spec's command-word appendix\npins the decision vocabulary definitions (SRC-SPEC-4CH1,\ninternational-gcse-chemistry-2017-specification.pdf p 52). Temporal scope:\nCURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
{"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "chunk_id": "PRO-04:rec:PRO-026", "content_sha256": "49884a8cf50c3eb7e3bc065af191d0fe80d5a358746e59a943ae9be1ec2b94e2", "heading": "PRO-026", "kind": "record", "metadata": {"artifact_id": "PRO-04", "artifact_version": 1.0, "curriculum_anchor_refs": [], "curriculum_version": "2017", "provenance": {"generation_run_id": "SIB-CHEMISTRY_4CH1-RUN-006", "generator": {"agent_version": "SIB-GEN-r0", "model": "GLM", "provider": "z.ai"}, "source_manifest": "SRC-QPMS-4CH1", "source_revisions": {"syllabai": "357ace0a230f5e0095ad230320af587dca6bb71f", "syllabai_pastpapers": "3b6a443d4e3643f461a1cca12c6e1ad47ab6b596", "syllabai_resources": "8b5a64f1b18724208ff19969b002028d3ed41bed"}}, "qualification": "International GCSE", "record_id": "PRO-026", "research_family": "problem_solving_intelligence", "source_scope": {"examiner_reports": false, "mark_schemes": true, "question_papers": true, "specification": true, "supplementary": false, "textbook": true}, "specification": "4CH1", "status": "PUBLISHED", "subject": "Chemistry", "temporal_scope": {"current": true, "legacy": false}}, "record_id": "PRO-026", "text": "### PRO-026 — Book-side decision rules\n\n**Claim:** the book teaches its own decision rules as three-region phase logic.\n**Evidence:** the states section fixes the rule — \"A substance is a solid at\ntemperatures below its melting point\", liquid between melting and boiling, gas\nabove boiling (SRC-BOOK-4CH1-SB1, edexcel_igcse_chemistry_chunks_v3.jsonl line\n33). Temporal scope: CURRENT — AUTHORITATIVE."}
